The Twilight Forest - modified SkyTekx build for Forge 1.20.1
============================================================

This is a MODIFIED version of The Twilight Forest.

Original work
-------------
  The Twilight Forest by TeamTwilight (originally by Benimatic)
  Source:   https://github.com/TeamTwilight/twilightforest
  Base:     branch 1.20.1 @ 1bc3a4c21213bc443967e92125613cb9ef47891e (Twilight Forest 4.3, Forge 47)
  Backport: content taken from branch 1.21.1 @ 9e40a75721c716b2fdf80c16d1058fe718825e9f
            (Twilight Forest 4.8, NeoForge 1.21.1)

Modifications
-------------
  Modified by SkyTekx (Florian Kleber), 2026, for the SkyTekx 3 modpack. The result still runs on
  Minecraft 1.20.1 with Forge 47, keeps the mod id twilightforest and is versioned
  4.3.2508-skytekx.1.

  Summary of the changes:
  - Twilight Forest 4.8 bugfixes, features and content backported onto the 4.3 code: crash,
    concurrency and multiplayer fixes; boss and mob reworks (Lich, Knight Phantom, Hydra, Ur-Ghast,
    multiplayer boss scaling); finished 4.3 work-in-progress items and blocks; new blocks and items;
    worldgen content for newly generated chunks (lakes, berry and oreberry bushes, hollow trees,
    fallen trunks, troll caves and more); the revamped Lich Tower; drying racks, foods and camps;
    Traveller's Gear and its modifiers; density-shaped landmark terrain; refreshed translations.
  - 1.21.1 APIs translated to 1.20.1 ones: Data Components became item stack NBT, Data Attachments
    became Forge capabilities and entity NBT, new packets are registered on the existing Forge
    SimpleChannel (with a protocol version bump), NeoForge data maps became datapack reload
    listeners, and copied 4.8 data uses the 1.20.1 folder names and formats.
  - Mystic Crown Compat (an MIT-licensed 1.21.1 addon by 741741) is integrated into the mod's own
    classes; see META-INF/NOTICE-mystic-crown-compat.txt.
  - Content that needs 1.21 game features is not included.

  The complete change history is the git history of the ports/twilightforest directory of
  https://github.com/skytekx/skytekx3-1201-server
  That directory is the source code of this jar: the exact source of a given jar is that directory
  at the commit that added the jar to local-mods/.

